      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pulmonary alveolar microlithiasis (PAM) is a rare autosomal recessive disease caused by mutations in SLC34A2 and characterized by intra-alveolar accumulation of microliths. We diagnosed a case of PAM in a 27-year-old Japanese female and identified a novel mutation in SLC34A2 (c.1390 G>C [G464R] in exon 12)."},
